+ * numbers its vertex input: an argument table holds
+ * KK_MAX_ARGUMENT_TABLE_BUFFERS buffer binds and MSL numbers an
+ * [[attribute(n)]] up to KK_MAX_NATIVE_VERTEX_ATTRIBS - 1.  The lowered fetch
+ * has neither limit, because it reads its buffers through the root descriptor
+ * table and indexes its own attribute array, so a binding or a location past
+ * Metal's end keeps that path and the advertised maxVertexInputBindings and
+ * maxVertexInputAttributes stand. */
